;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-1y3.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-1 3)
  title: "First Sight"
  intent: "the scree's last shoulder over the mist, where the whole glazed wood glitters below: a breath"
  bed: (wind 0.7 water 0.1 hum 0.1)
  grid:
  ("##                       "
   "##                       "
   "##                       "
   "##                       "
   "##                       "
   "##                       "
   "##           %%%%%%%%%%%%"
   "##           %%%%%%%%%%%%"
   "##           %%%%%%%%%%%%"
   "##           %%%%%%%%%%%%"
   "##           ############")
  decor: auto)
;; The shoulder (columns 13-24) ends over nothing: stand at its lip and
;; the whole wood is below. West of the lip the ground falls away
;; (columns 2-12) into the Icicle Walk. Nothing joins the Branch Stair to
;; the west (columns 0-1 are rock to the sky). Its moment, the-ice-rings
;; (first visit), is named when SOUND writes the tune.
